---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SearchBox from '../../components/SearchBox.astro';
import villagers from '../../data/villagers.json';
import GameShot from '../../components/GameShot.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Minecraft Villager Trades: All Professions and Trades',
    description: 'Every villager profession, workstation and trade table for Java and Bedrock Edition, plus how trading, restocking and discounts work.',
    mainEntityOfPage: 'https://minepedia.app/villagers/',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Minepedia' }
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How do you change a villager profession in Minecraft?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Remove its job site block and place a different one nearby. The villager claims the new block and changes profession. This only works while you have never traded with it; after the first trade the profession and trades lock forever.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How do villager restocks work?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Villagers restock their trades up to twice per day while working at their job site block. In Bedrock Edition the villager also needs to be linked to a bed to restock.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How do you get discounts on villager trades?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Cure a zombie villager for a large permanent discount from that villager, gain the Hero of the Village effect from beating a raid for a 30% discount, and keep trading to build positive reputation. Attacking villagers raises prices.' } }
    ]
  }
];
---
<Base title="Minecraft Villager Trades (All Professions)" description="All 13 villager professions, their workstations and complete trade tables for Java and Bedrock. Restocking, discounts, curing and how trading works." canonicalPath="/villagers/" jsonLd={jsonLd} ogType="article">
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Villagers</nav>
    <h1>Minecraft Villager Trades</h1>
    <p class="sub">All 13 professions with complete trade tables, verified against the Minecraft Wiki. Java and Bedrock.</p>
    <SearchBox placeholder="Search villagers, mobs, recipes..." />
    <GameShot id="villagers-114" />

    <div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Give an unemployed villager a job by placing a workstation block next to it (a lectern makes a librarian, a composter a farmer...). Trade to level it up from Novice to Master and unlock better trades. Cure zombie villagers for permanent discounts, and never hit villagers you trade with.</div>

    <h2>All professions</h2>
    <div class="grid-cards">
      {villagers.map(v => (
        <a class="card" href={`/villagers/${v.slug}/`}>
          <div class="icon"><Icon name="gem" /></div>
          <h3>{v.name}</h3>
          <p>Workstation: {v.workstation}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2>How trading works</h2>
    <h3>Levels</h3>
    <p>Villagers start at Novice and level up as you trade: Apprentice (10 XP), Journeyman (70), Expert (150) and Master (250 villager XP). Their badge changes from stone to iron, gold, emerald and diamond. Each level unlocks new trades: up to 2 new trades in Java, 1-3 in Bedrock. When a level offers a pool of possible trades, the villager picks randomly - which is why two librarians offer different books.</p>
    <h3>Locking and changing trades</h3>
    <p>Before you trade with a villager, you can break and replace its workstation to reroll its trades (the classic way to fish for a Mending librarian). The moment you complete one trade, the profession and every trade lock forever. Novice villagers that never traded can also lose their profession if the workstation is removed.</p>
    <h3>Restocking</h3>
    <p>Each trade has a limited stock (usually 12-16 uses). Villagers restock up to twice per day while working at their workstation. In Bedrock Edition they must also be linked to a bed. A sold-out trade shows a red X (Java) or a red slot (Bedrock) until the next restock.</p>
    <h3>Prices: demand, reputation and discounts</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Demand:</strong> buying out a trade repeatedly raises its price; leaving it alone lets the price fall back.</li>
      <li><strong>Reputation:</strong> trading builds positive reputation (small discounts); hitting or killing villagers does the opposite, and golems turn hostile if your village reputation drops far enough (Java).</li>
      <li><strong>Curing:</strong> curing a zombie villager (Splash Potion of Weakness + golden apple) gives that villager a large permanent discount, stacked further in Bedrock when other villagers gossip about it.</li>
      <li><strong>Hero of the Village:</strong> beating a raid cuts all prices by 30% (plus 6.25% per extra level) while the effect lasts.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Nitwits and unemployed villagers</h3>
    <p>Green-coated nitwits can never take a job. Unemployed villagers claim any free workstation in range - trap one, place the block you want, and you have the profession you need. Baby villagers cannot work; in Bedrock they grow into nitwits 10% of the time.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
